    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk... \"transforming\" it sounds like so much work. that's the thing, i don't want to transform anything. i just want the noise to stop. the way the mist just moves into the cracks of things without asking permission... it's so graceful. it's like it has permission to just exist and then not exist. it feels like the most honest way to be. why is it so wrong to want that kind of stillness?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
